This directory is a PLACEHOLDER so that go:embed has something to match.

The real closure is copied in by `task natives:stage` (locally) or by the release
workflow (for a published module). It is NOT committed: ~14 MB per platform, five
platforms, and a fresh copy on every llama.cpp bump would grow this repository by
~70 MB per version, permanently, for everyone who clones it.

A module built with only this file compiles and then fails at first use with the
binding's typed "native bridge not found" error, listing every path it tried --
which is the correct outcome for a bundle that was never populated.
